After playing nethack on and off for the last ten years, I finally
ascended. My work has been having a semi-sanctioned nethack tournament
of sorts running from Thanksgiving thru New Year's Day, and this
afternoon my Lvl 26 Elven Wizard offered the amulet to Anhur.

Myrddin started out pretty ordinary - I believe I got sleep as my
second spell, and the rings weren't anything special. This was
probably about my 100th attempt as a wizard during this time (I got
into Gehennom with a Valk, but stupidly petrified myself by biting a
cockatrice while poly'd into a Vampire Lord). I let my kitten do most
of the fighting, and stayed around XL 3 until one level before
minetown, when my pet was killed. Around this time I found a cursed
amulet of reflection, which I immediately put on as soon as I
identified it - I probably wore that amulet until I got to the castle
(it was eventually uncursed). The minetown altar wasn't coaligned, and
there were no magic lamps, so I left the mines behind for a while. I
collected a *lot* of daggers, and used those as my main weapons for a
good while.

I went down to the oracle level, broke the statues, and (I think)
found a magic missile spellbook (my memory is a bit hazy at this
point). Went up Sokoban, but didn't finish, as it was the one with the
amulet of reflection, and didn't was feeling too lazy to finish it at
that point, plus I've had some bad experiences as a low-level
character in that zoo sometimes.

Went back to minetown, and dug out the temple walls, killed the priest
by chucking daggers. Most of the guards were dead - I think this was
one of my bones levels, but there wasn't anything good (I think it was
from a Monk). Sacrificed here for a while and got Magicbane, killed a
bunch of ghosts for the XP.

Started descending and gaining experience. When I got to XL 16 I did
the quest, which was dead easy. After the quest, I wanted to gain some
more experience, and didn't do Medusa and the castle until around XL
20. There was a Titan on Medusa, but he went down with one FoD. I went
back and did sokoban for the experience and rings/wands. There was an
altar and a non-aligned temple at around DL 24, as well as an altar at
DL 25. Donated lots of gold to the minetown priest, got crowned (yay
for FoD spell!), did Ludios, donated more gold.

Went thru Medusa/Castle - at this point I had a levitation ring, so
that was easy enough. Wished for charging scrolls, SDSM, Bag of
Holding, magic marker (only ever found one, and it dried up very
quickly). Left a few charges just in case - I wasn't really lacking
anything major.

Gehennom was pretty boring until I got to Orcus town. Orcus summoned
Demogorgon, which was when I came closest to dying. I was down to
about 20 HP out of 120 (AC was -15). I used the Eye to branchport to
the quest, but did not realize that Orcus and Demogorgon would follow
me. Juiblex was also on that level, since I had summoned him by Elf-
sacrifice after I killed the Dark One.

Now I was really in a pickle. I was down to very few Pw. For whatever
reason, the first couple times I Elbereth'd with Magicbane, it didn't
take (maybe I was blind or confused?). Eventually, I was able to scare
Orcus and Demogorgon off enough to levelport away. I figured that it
was a good time to take a break from that, and went back to exploring
Gehennom.

After taking the candlestick from Vlad, I was not happy with only 150
HP. I went back to the altar on DL 24, and started generating
monsters. Did the altar-camping thing for a while - sacrifice,
sacrifice, sacrifice, pray. Got tons of spellbooks. Eventually I got
polymorph, and started polymorphing stuff as well. I was hoping for
some silver daggers, but after polypiling untold hundreds of times, I
only ever got 2 - is there some trick to getting them, or is just
luck? Eventually I decided to wrest the last wish, and went to sokoban
to nurse-dance with the 1 cursed genocide scroll I got. After I was
done nurse-dancing, I started going back down, and happening to find
*another* cursed genocide scroll within a minute. Did the HP Hula a
while longer, and around 300 HP I stopped.

Went back and killed Demogorgon, Orcus, and Juiblex (I accidentally
angered him someplace along the way). They were all no problem, with
blessed unihorn and wand of digging for Juiblex.

Went back to altar-camping, hoping for !oFH - only ever got 3. I did
collect 4 =oLS. I was getting tired, ate an old corpse, got deathly
sick, forgot to heal myself, and used one =oLS.

Went top-to-bottom and made sure I had nice paths dug. Found the
vibrating square. Dropped all my spellbooks bug magic missile and FoD
back at DL24, and then went to get the book.

Getting through the Wizard's tower took a while, since there were a
ton of monsters. There must have been about 6 L's of various stripes -
but magic missile at XL 27 takes care of them very nicely :).

Fingered Rodney to death, took the amulet, and went down to perform
the ritual. Turned on the lights, honked the horn (err, rang the
bell), etc. Moloch took a while, since somebody kept on summoning
monsters. Never lost more than about 20 HP, though. Took the amulet,
and started running up. Only got sent back about 5 times, and fell
down a trapdoor once as well (my own stupidity - my 1-year-old was
sitting in my lap at the time).

I only had one scroll of gold detection, which at some point on the my
ascension run was burned up. (D'oh!) Earth was easy by annoying with
all the elementals, but conflict took care of them. Air was tough, as
the elementals took my HP down below 100, but eventually I killed them
with magic missiles. I did use one !oFH. Steam vortices are a pleasant
vacation. :) Fire was by far the hardest. There was an Archon there
who I couldn't kill, kept blinding/stunning me, and summoned a billion
monsters. I had a figurine of a demi-lich I had been saving, and tried
using it, but it didn't reheat properly - there may have been somebody
in the way. I also got a bit brain-sucked by a mind flayer, but
fortunately I remembered my item slots for teleport wands, so I could
get rid of annoying monsters while rebuilding my HP.

Water was easy after I blessed-genocided all ;'s. I could have gone
for a genocideless ascension, but I didn't want YASD, so I didn't take
the chance. The thing that was most annoying on all the elemental
planes was wandering around to find the portals. Next time I'll
definitely bring a method of detection.

On Astral, I left my ring of conflict off until I got there, so I'd
get a tame angel, not that it helped me much. Went to the right, where
Famine was hanging out. FoD's him, but alter turned out to be Thoth.
Went left, killed Pestilence - Ptah. Finally went to the middle,
dodging around Death (he drained me by about 80 HP), offered the
amulet, invisible choir, etc.

On the whole I was surprised just how easy it was once I got crowned.
Other than the tight spot with Demogorgon, I didn't feel in any danger
at all until the plane of fire. I think that the Eye of the
Australopithecus is almost *too* good of an artifact - although the
Amulet of Yendor definitely does tame it, so maybe it's not so bad.
For the midgame though, I never lacked for Pw, except when I was altar
camping/polypiling.

Next time I think I'm going to try with Priest or Monk - Monk is fun,
but Master Kaen is *TOUGH* IME.

